abode abided\Usually follows 'can' when it means 'put up with'arose arisen\awoke awoken\bore borne\The past participle is 'born' when the meaning is 'give birth to a child' beat beaten\became become\befell befallen\begot begotten\began begun\beheld beheld\bent bent\bereft bereft\Usually passive besought besought\beset beset\Usually passivebestrode bestridden\bet bet\betook betaken\bethought bethought\Usually reflexivebade bidden\There is also the past tense 'I bid' and perfect 'I have bid' in games like Bridgebound bound\bit bitten\bled bled\The transitive sense is now usually metaphorical as in 'They are bleeding me dry' (taking my money)blew blown\broke broken\bred bred\brought brought\broadcast broadcast\built built\burst burst\bought bought\cast cast\caught caught\chid chidden\chose chosen\clove cloven\clung clung\came come\cost cost\'Cost' in this sense has a complement rather than an objectcrept crept\crew crowed\cut cut\dealt dealt\dug dug\did done\drew drawn\drank drunk\drove driven\ate eaten\fell fallen\fed fed\felt felt\fought fought\found found\flew flown\forbore forborne\forbade forbidden\forecast forecast\foresaw foreseen\foretold foretold\forgot forgotten\forgave forgiven\forsook forsaken\forswore forsworn\froze frozen\gainsaid gainsaid\got got\The US past participle is 'gotten'gave given\went gone\ground ground\grew grown\hung hung\had had\heard heard\hid hidden\hit hit\held held\hurt hurt\input input\kept kept\knelt knelt\knew known\laid laid\led led\left left\lent lent\let let\lay lain\lit lit\lost lost\made made\meant meant\met met\miscast miscast\misdealt misdealt\misgave misgiven\mishit mishit\mislaid mislaid\misled misled\misspent misspent\mistook mistaken\misunderstood misunderstood\mowed mown\offset offset\outdid outdone\outgrew outgrown\output output\outran outrun\outshone outshone\overbid overbid\overcame overcome\overdid overdone\overdrew overdrawnoverate overeaten\overfed overfed\overflew overflown\overhung overhung\overlay overlain\overpa