 followed by TO verbmay be followed by TO verb or verbING with the same meaningThis verb is common in the passive followed by ATusually followed by FORfollowed by TO VERB in sense 1 and by VERB-ING in sense 3HAPPEN can have a personal subject when followed by a TO infinitive as in `She happened to see me'.OCCUR may have a personal subject in sense (2), as in `He occurred to me as a likely suspect'.usually followed by FORnormally with OUT OF ...usually followed by offorewent foregone\lipread lipread\forwent forgone\alternative spelling of foregooverwrote overwritten\underwrote underwritten\restrang restrung\lip-read lip-read\alternative spelling of lipreadmost common as a phrasal verb: tool upalways followed by a phrase with ONfled fled\usually intransitive but transitive in set phrases such as 'fled the scene' or 'flee the coop'.